      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x.$",
      "worked_solution": "We calculate the derivative using the product rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x) \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cdot (-{csc}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x{cot}^{2}⁡x-{csc}^{3}⁡x\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
